brand: Never Summer
model name: Easy Rider
model year: 2027
gender: Mens
AUD price: $999.99
availability: Pre-order (Estimated June 1, 2026)
available lengths: 152cm, 154cm, 157cm, 158cm Wide, 160cm Wide
board type: Freestyle-All Mountain
flex: 5/10 (1=soft, 10=stiff)
flex description: Mid-flex, balanced blend of flexibility and stiffness, versatile for all-mountain riding, responsive for carving with forgiveness for playful riding
rider level: Intermediate
shape: Twin (symmetrical tip to tail, equal performance riding forward or switch)
camber type: Triple Camber Hybrid with R.I.P. Edge Hold Technology
camber description: Overall central rocker shape with camber zone between, creating two high-pressure rocker sections on each side of a middle camber. Increases edge efficiency, outstanding responsiveness, stability, effortless float, playful and forgiving ride, explosive pop, and butterability.
edge hold technology: R.I.P. Edge Hold Technology (waves integrated into the base creating high-pressure points for smooth drag-free rides and consistent pressure on edge, unlike traditional serrated edges)
width: Standard, Wide
sidecut type: Power Grip Sidecut (multiple radii creating additional contact points, flat section in middle area, two shallow radii on either side, deeper radii near tips for quick turn initiation)
mounting pattern: 2x4 inserts
topsheet: Co-Extruded Polymer Topsheet (tough lightweight thermoplastic with fiber backing, scratch/chip resistant, vivid colors, built-in stomp pad grip)
laminate: Bi-Lite Fiberglass, Carbon Max Laminate Technology, STS Pre-Tensioned Fiberglass
laminate detail - Bi-Lite Fiberglass: Lightweight glass fiber matrix for outstanding freestyle and freeride performance
laminate detail - Carbon Max: Strategically layered carbon matrix reinforcing key areas for strength, responsiveness, and energy transfer
laminate detail - STS Pre-Tensioned Fiberglass: Elastomer stringers between glass fibers to improve strength and edge hold
core material: NS SuperLight Wood Core (Poplar, Paulownia, and Birch combination, lightweight yet sturdy, universal flex)
core woods: Poplar, Paulownia, Birch
damping system: Triple Layer RDS 2 Damping with Underfoot Stabiliser
damping description - RDS 2: Balance between freeride stability and freestyle responsiveness, more damping than typical freestyle board, slightly less than dedicated freeride board
underfoot stabiliser: Elastomeric Underfoot Stabilisers (positioned beneath mounting area for shock/vibration absorption, high-speed stability, extra cushioning to minimise foot fatigue)
sidewall material: UHMW Sidewalls (Ultra High Molecular Weight Polyethylene, more resistant to cracking in cold temperatures than ABS, improved damping around metal edges)
edge: Fullwrap Metal Edge
base: Durasurf XT Sintered 5501 Base (high performance sintered base infused with graphite, fast and durable)
additional feature 1: Extended Transition Area
additional feature 2: Low Profile Nose/Tail
additional feature 3: P-Tex Nose/Tail Protection
